# starexch555 -- MULTI-ID WAGER (knockout tournament) tab.
# Run: .venv/bin/python tournament_runner.py --env .env.starexch.tournament
# Sheet columns: USERNAME | PASSWORD | START BALANCE | BALANCE | STAGE OUT | RESULT
# Control cell I1: type START to launch a run.
#
# ⚠️ NOT READY YET. starexch's Live Casino entry point is a
# <div data-href="/live-casino">, not cricmatch's <a>, so open_casino_lobby()
# does not match it and sites/starexch.py keeps supports_casino=False. The
# tournament will refuse cleanly until that path is captured live.
BOT_SITE_URL=https://starexch555.com
SETTINGS_FILE=bot_settings.starexch.json

TOURNAMENT_SPREADSHEET_ID=your-spreadsheet-id-from-the-sheet-url
# TODO: replace with the real gid of the multi-id wager tab.
TOURNAMENT_WORKSHEET_GID=448123374
TOURNAMENT_CREDENTIALS_FILE=service_account.json

TOURNAMENT_GROUP_SIZE=10

# How many GROUPS play at the same time. Every pair inside one group already
# bets on the same hand, so this is the only serial part left: groups used to
# be played one after another, which is where a 100-account run spent 6-7
# hours. The machine ends up running GROUP_SIZE x this many browsers at once,
# so raise it only as far as this box has RAM for -- start at 2. Logins stay
# paced globally, so lanes do NOT multiply the login rate.
TOURNAMENT_PARALLEL_GROUPS=1

# Hard cap on browsers open AT ONCE across all lanes (group_size x lanes).
# The runner clamps lanes to fit under it. Exists because a 2026-08-23 run
# with 30 browsers at once went blind on every table for 94 minutes -- the
# box, not the site, was the ceiling. Raise only after probe_seat_decay.py
# shows this machine holding more seats healthily.
TOURNAMENT_MAX_SEATS=12

# Play at a table from Evolution's own in-game lobby instead of Baccarat A.
# Find candidates with probe_lobby_tables.py; a table whose smallest chip is
# Rs 10 drains a loser in ONE hand (fewer hands = faster run) and cuts the
# leftover an eliminated account keeps from up to Rs 99 to at most Rs 9.
# The chip rail is read LIVE off the first seat and verified before any bet.
# Remember to set TOURNAMENT_TABLE_MIN to match the table.
#TOURNAMENT_LOBBY_TILE=Speed Baccarat A
# Now that the pacer queues PER EXIT IP, this is per proxy, not global -- with
# five proxies, 5 here means one login per IP every 25s, safer than the old
# global 20s and it seats ten browsers in 50s instead of 200s. Seating fast
# matters on its own: a seat's grip on the table decays with age (see
# CLAUDE.md), so a group that takes 200s to seat starts half dead.
TOURNAMENT_LOGIN_SPACING=5
TOURNAMENT_TABLE_MIN=100
TOURNAMENT_TABLE_MAX=200000
# Its OWN state file -- two tournament instances sharing one would silently
# erase each other's record (see CLAUDE.md).
TOURNAMENT_STATE_FILE=tournament_state.starexch.json
TOURNAMENT_CONTROL_CELL=I1
TOURNAMENT_CONTROL_LABEL_CELL=H1
